<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson signs 220 mln skr Hungary deal.</title>
<headline>Ericsson signs 220 mln skr Hungary deal.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group AB LM Ericsson said on Wednesday it had signed an agreement to expand Westel 900's GSM network in Hungary.</p>
<p>The agreement, worth 220 million crowns, will include deliveries and installation of switching and radio equipment for the whole country.</p>
<p>&quot;This means that Ericsson will remain as Westel 900's sole supplier for GSM equipment,&quot; Ericsson said in a statement.</p>
<p>Deliveries are scheduled from February 1997.</p>
<p>Westel 900 is Hungary's leading GSM operator with its network already covering 90 percent of Hungary and over 95 percent of the population.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1045</p>
